  <h2 id="lossy-vs-lossless">Lossy vs Lossless Compression</h2>
  <p>The debate between MP3 and WAV boils down to one fundamental concept in digital media: compression.</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>WAV is Lossless and Uncompressed:</strong> It keeps all the original audio data. It is a perfect, 1:1 digital replica of the studio recording. </li>
    <li><strong>MP3 is Lossy:</strong> To make the file size smaller, the MP3 encoder throws away audio data that the human ear struggles to hear (like extreme high frequencies or very quiet sounds masked by loud ones). This "loss" is permanent.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="comparison">Comparison</h2>
  
  <ComparisonTable 
    caption="MP3 vs WAV Quick Comparison"
