      ['Audio Quality', 'Good (Perfect for everyday listening)', 'Perfect (Studio reference quality)'],
      ['File Size', 'Small (~5MB per song)', 'Massive (~50MB per song)'],
      ['Best For', 'Streaming, Phones, USB Drives', 'Music Production, Video Editing']
    ]}
  />

  <h2 id="which-to-choose">Which Should You Choose?</h2>
  <p>If you are downloading a podcast, an audiobook, or music to listen to on your phone during a commute, <strong>choose MP3</strong>. The file size is tiny, it plays on everything, and you won't notice the missing audio data on standard headphones.</p>
  <p>If you are downloading a sound effect to use in a video editing project, or if you are an audio professional archiving a recording, <strong>choose WAV</strong>. You want the highest possible quality source file before you begin editing and exporting.</p>
